# A downed teammate is helped up through the game's own hold prompt over their body, never by just standing there.
# The agent cannot hold a key, so `helpup` finishes the hold the way the game does once the bar fills.

include session.coop
# The host's stand-near option is a saved preference: off for the default rule, whatever a failed run left.
A standnear off

A tp 20,1170
B tp 60,1170
A expect teammate <= 100 timeout=10

# ---- Standing over a downed player does nothing; the prompt shows on the helper's machine only. ----
B hit me 5000
B expect ai me contains mode=KnockOut timeout=5
A expect interactables LootKnockout 200 contains LootKnockout timeout=5
B expect interactables LootKnockout 200 == none timeout=1
sleep 3
B expect ai me contains mode=KnockOut timeout=1
B expect counter helpedup <= 0 timeout=1

# ---- The host helps the client up; the prompt goes with the knockout. ----
A helpup
B expect counter helpedup >= 1 timeout=5
B expect ai me !contains mode=KnockOut timeout=5
A expect ai DrovaCoop.Remote !contains mode=KnockOut timeout=10
A expect interactables LootKnockout 200 == none timeout=5

# ---- The client helps the host up, through the host-routed message. ----
sleep 3
A hit me 5000
A expect ai me contains mode=KnockOut timeout=5
B expect interactables LootKnockout 200 contains LootKnockout timeout=5
B helpup
A expect counter helpedup >= 1 timeout=5
A expect ai me !contains mode=KnockOut timeout=5
B expect interactables LootKnockout 200 == none timeout=5

# ---- A late help on a player already up does nothing. ----
B helpup
sleep 1
A expect counter helpedup <= 1 timeout=1

# ---- The host's option: standing over a downed teammate gets them up too, without the prompt. ----
A standnear on
sleep 2
B hit me 5000
B expect ai me contains mode=KnockOut timeout=5
A tp 50,1170
B expect counter helpedup >= 2 timeout=6
B expect ai me !contains mode=KnockOut timeout=5
A standnear off
